From 5a8cb39eb94e128d861e9af3861038c1ff202d8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:21:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: an openssl CertificateGenerator with SubjectAltName
 support

The GHSA-vvx9 tests generate certificates with DNS, SRV, URI and IP
SANs. 5.6 has no CertificateGenerator.inc at all. This adds the one of
later branches: SHA-256 (accepted at security level 2), SAN support
through a temporary config file, and bug68265/bug68879/san_peer_matching
on generated certificates instead of the stored .pem files (deleted).
Test change only.

Sury's 5.6 patches 0302 (the 7.2 generator) and 0308 (no trailing comma
in calls), with backports of php-src 52c2f1126d, c7fe71c8b7 and
21a2da2349 (Nikita Popov), his 0303-0305.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
